Hi Phil,

Thanks for all your help, sorry to bother you again. I reran with a fit for multipleGroups as:

multipleGroup(data=data[,-1],1,group=data[,1])

> multipleGroup(data=data[,-1],1,group=data[,1])
Iteration: 500, Log-Lik: -3720.647, Max-Change: 0.00149
EM cycles terminated after 500 iterations.

Call:
multipleGroup(data = data[, -1], model = 1, group = data[, 1])

Full-information item factor analysis with 1 factor(s).

FAILED TO CONVERGE within 1e-04 tolerance after 500 EM iterations.
mirt version: 1.28

M-step optimizer: BFGS
EM acceleration: Ramsay
Number of rectangular quadrature: 61

Latent density type: Gaussian

Log-likelihood = -3720.647
Estimated parameters: 136
AIC = 7713.294; AICc = 8197.242
BIC = 8171.067; SABIC = 7740.117

The DIF now returns, here Gender again is a separate reference file with character gender, I tried also with the Gender column identified in the same data sheet and get the same result:

> DIF(MGmodel, Gender$Gender)
No hyper-parameters were estimated in the DIF model. For effective
                 DIF testing, freeing the focal group hyper-parameters is recommended.
Error: Item 1 does not contain any of the parameters defined in which.par.
                 Consider removing it from the item2test input or adding relevant parameters
                 to which.par

Best,

Jack

