Phil,

Convergence problems disappeared after N was set to 10 000 as opposed to 1 000. Thank you.

Looking at the parameters recovered. d is estimated quite well but a values are off.

I think it has to do with your last comment below.

This model is unique only up to a linear transformation, so you'd need to do a rotation after the model has converged in order to recover the original parameter structure.

How can I do this? Can you help? I thought you meant that I should get the loadings output by summary() to do that, but the output is the same regardless of the rotation setting.

> summary(mirt.fit)
> summary(mirt.fit,rotation="oblimin")
> summary(mirt.fit,rotation="varimax")

Note that rather than using your for() loops you could use the simdata() function from mirt, which will generate data much faster. HTH.

I was aware of the existence of the simdata() but I wanted to give it a try myself for the sake of control. Thank you!

Regards,

Hugo

